 "proved": "No printed total/grand-total row exists on this page to check against. The page does imply a per-row identity (Forward + Commitments + Refunds + Abatements + Payments + Transfer + Adjustments = Balances, standard for a receivables summary), which I checked wherever a row had all its contributing figures present in the OCR. It held EXACTLY for: Real Estate Levy of 2024 (475,974.40); Motor Vehicle Excise Levy of 2011, 2022, 2023, and 2024 (all reconciled to the cent). It did NOT hold, and could not be resolved, for most other Real Estate and Personal Property rows because their Forward and/or Commitments boxes are simply absent from the OCR even where the printed Balance implies a nonzero Forward must exist (e.g. Real Estate Levy of 2023: Refunds+Abatements+Payments+Transfer alone give −396,634.12 against a printed Balance of −8,081.96; a missing Forward of ~388,552.16 would close it, but that figure is not in the OCR given, so it is left blank rather than invented). Personal Property Levy of 2024 is a specific flagged anomaly: 936,789.35 sits at x=0.442, which is nearest the ABATEMENTS column cluster (0.442–0.447) and is placed there per the nearest-centre rule, but the identity only closes if that figure is read as COMMITMENTS instead (936,789.35 − 906,815.12 = 29,974.23, exact). Not silently reassigned.",
 "note": "Two header cells in the OCR are each a merged run of multiple column words at one reported x-coordinate: \"COMMITIMENTS[sic] ABATEMENTS\" at x=0.353, and \"TRANSFER ADJUSTMENTS BALANCES\" at x=0.684. I split these into their constituent printed words (COMMITMENTS, ABATEMENTS; TRANSFER, ADJUSTMENTS, BALANCES) and located each one's true column position from where the data figures themselves cluster in x (COMMITMENTS ≈0.36–0.38, ABATEMENTS ≈0.44–0.45, TRANSFER ≈0.684 exact, ADJUSTMENTS ≈0.759 exact, BALANCES ≈0.84–0.85), then confirmed the split against the arithmetic identity on complete rows (see `proved`). \"BALANCE FORWARD\" is likely the full header for the \"FORWARD\" column but only that one word was OCR'd. The FORWARD column is fully populated for Motor Vehicle Excise but almost entirely missing from the OCR for Real Estate and Personal Property, even on rows whose nonzero Balance implies one exists — a genuine OCR coverage gap, not zero activity, so those cells were left blank rather than back-solved. TRANSFER and ADJUSTMENTS each have exactly one value on the whole page. One cell (Personal Property, Levy of 2024, 936,789.35) has an ambiguous column per the conflict between nearest-x placement and the identity check; flagged in `proved` rather than resolved by guessing."
